# What each gate reads, for attest fingerprints (attest SPEC, "Input fingerprints").
#
# A gate is covered on any tree whose declared paths are byte-identical to the
# tree it passed on, so the closing plan commit (docs/plans only) reuses every
# result. The grammar cannot exclude paths: this lists every tracked top-level
# path and every docs/ child except docs/plans. `amont attest check-inputs`
# (make attest-inputs) fails when a tracked file is not covered, for any gate.
#
# `.github` is declared whole on purpose: ci.yaml is an input of every gate, so
# a change to a tool install invalidates the signatures.
